            <div class="book-intro-content" id="bookIntroContent">
                <h2>King's Cross from below</h2>
                <p><p><strong>40 years of community action around King's Cross developments</strong><br>
                Edited by Michael Edwards and Jason Katz<br>
                A book published by UCL Press, 2026</p>
                
                <p>King's Cross from below is an open-access academic book documenting four decades of community action around the redevelopment of King's Cross in London. The book brings together 36 contributors – activists, residents, planners, and scholars – to tell the story of how communities engaged with, resisted, and shaped one of London's most significant urban transformations.</p>
                
                <p>This website serves as a living archive for the book. It is published by Michael Edwards and Jason Katz and will be preserved as part of the British Library's digital archive. Each chapter has a permanent URL for citation purposes. The website provides an accessible, archival-quality format designed for both online reading and printing.</n
                <p><strong>How to cite pages from this site:</strong> Author Name(s). "Page Title." In <em>King's Cross from below</em>, edited by Michael Edwards and Jason Katz. Companion website. [Permanent URL]. Accessed [Date].</p>
            </div>
        </div>

